{"phase":"types","diagnostics":[{"code":"E0609","name":"literal-captures","phase":"types","root":1,"at":{"file":"m/00.mk","line":6,"col":43,"end_line":6,"end_col":44},"message":"a `fn` literal that reads `k` is no value: only a literal written directly as the argument of a `const` parameter may read the enclosing function's locals (here it is passed to a `const` parameter whose type is not a `fn` type, which the callee may use as any value); to store a callback, store a `fn` value and its plain state; see the cookbook's stored-callback recipe","facts":{"captured":["k"],"reason":"argument","literal":"m/00.mk:6:14"},"fixes":[],"alternatives":["a struct holding what the callback needs, and a named `fn` that takes it","a loop instead of the callback"],"explain":"mk explain E0609"}],"omitted":0}
